# Command clone-website

## What does this command do:

Clone any website with one command using AI coding agents

## Installed from

For Fedora install using:
```
git clone https://github.com/JCodesMore/ai-website-cloner-template.git \
  ~/Projects/3rd-party-repos/ai-website-cloner-template
cd ~/Projects/3rd-party-repos/ai-website-cloner-template && npm install
curl -sSfL <this-script> -o ~/.local/bin/clone-website && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/clone-website
```

The wrapper script at ~/.local/bin/clone-website cds into the project and runs `claude --chrome`.

## Command path

For Fedora run: /home/kinscoe/.local/bin/clone-website

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://github.com/JCodesMore/ai-website-cloner-template

## Command options

```
clone-website [claude-options]
```

Launches Claude Code with Chrome MCP enabled inside the ai-website-cloner-template project
directory. Any extra arguments are passed through to `claude`.

Once the Claude session opens, run the skill:

```
/clone-website <url1> [<url2> ...]
```

### Pipeline phases

1. Reconnaissance   — screenshots, design token extraction, interaction sweep
2. Foundation       — fonts, colors, globals, asset downloads
3. Component Specs  — spec files written to docs/research/components/
4. Parallel Build   — builder agents dispatched in git worktrees per section
5. Assembly & QA    — merge worktrees, wire page.tsx, visual diff vs original

### Requirements

- Node.js 24+
- Claude Code with Chrome MCP (`--chrome` flag)
- Project deps installed: cd ~/Projects/3rd-party-repos/ai-website-cloner-template && npm install
